{
  "about": "navigation_robot's field classes for the house ledger (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, L-WATCH part 2; WP-D navigation_robot). 'fields' classify every property of house_sim/data/types/navigation_robot.json (and the fields this domain's verbs and systems write on its own types) by name, for the types this domain defines; 'types' refine one type; a dotted name is one sub-key of a dict field, '<head>.*' every other sub-key. Classes: placement, setting, condition (worse: true / false / up / down), identity, content (guard 'mess': a load the mess balance judges), process, bookkeeping (kernel/ledger.py, watch_fields.json). The household robot's rv record: its run state, charging, errors and timers are driven by its own state machine (process); its bin is a debris load (content, mess: VERIFY_HARDENING 6.5, the vacuum class accepts debris), its tank content; hair on the brushes, a broken bumper switch, a damaged tank and a pad-damaged floor are conditions; its schedule is a setting; counters and derived flags are bookkeeping. A spare robot pack's record follows the physical pack the robot swaps in and out (swap_battery writes the old pack's charge, capacity, health and temperature onto it), so its capacity and health are process fields there; a damaged pack is marked by its swollen / damaged conditions. Water-sensitive: the electronic types (robot vacuums and their docks, the headlamp, the laser meter, the digital level, the robot pack and its charger, the elevator panels); the mower and its dock are weather-rated (waterproof) but inherit robot_vacuum / robot_vacuum_dock (a type-name rule: see the handoff's request to WP1).",
